the passport is the foundation for  modern global travel to get from one  country to another  you need one so not surprisingly  terrorists and criminals and fugitives  have been trying to get their hands on  stolen passports for a long time in 1980  ICAO established the basic standard for  all passports currently in circulation  it had four main features in the upper  right hand corner a unique identifying  number in the middle some basic  biographic data about the person holding  the passport at the bottom the same data  in machine readable form and most  importantly on the left a standard  picture in the old days it was fairly  easy for a criminal to travel on a  stolen Passport  as long as he or she fit the basic  physical description of the person they  stole it from the most important thing  to do was to replace the photograph and  since on old passports the photograph  merely consisted of a physical  photograph covered by lamination all  they had to do was cut the photograph  out replace it and they could travel it  after 9/11 it became clear that the  international community needed a better  passport starting in August 2007 every  new passport issued by the United States  is a modern epass port this new passport  has a number of features which makes  fraud almost impossible first notice the  photograph it's now on the first page of  the document and it's literally embedded  into the page itself so if you cut it  out will be easy to detect by an  official second every page of the  document has sophisticated and distinct  watermarking making it almost impossible  to dr. third embedded in the cover of  the passport is an RFID chip it contains  all the basic information on the  passport itself as well as a digital  picture that matches the picture in the  passports first page ie passports should  be fully phased in among all developed  countries by 2018 by then traveling on a  stolen Passport  will require a lot more than a scalpel a  new photograph and some lamination  [Music]
 

